Subject: [PATCH 02979/11362] [outer-loop] spec .415/.416 task: CNN
 frame-change/clickability predictor (the leaderboard's #1 technique)

Specs the highest-leverage steal from the competitive intel: a CNN action-effect predictor (the
Tufa StochasticGoose / Blind Squirrel core idea) that ranks the explorer's candidate actions by
predicted frame-change -> action efficiency, the scoring metric we have NONE of at 0.08. Trained
self-supervised on the (frame, action, next_frame) transitions we already generate, pooled across
games. Falsifiable gate: held-out actions-to-first-levelup strictly lower than blind BFS, no
solve-rate drop, positive control + null guard. Secondary: hidden-field probing in the state hash
(the competitor's fix for our ka59/ar25 deepening stall). Queued via known-issues MANDATORY-NEXT +
GAP-ARCH-FRAME-CHANGE-PREDICTOR + full spec note. Complements (not replaces) the verifier-energy thesis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
